{"id": "p05-8db71d8b-9028", "text": "第一步读取配置，第二步建立连接，第三步发起请求。每一步都依赖上一步的结果。三步走完就算完成一次调用。", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 50, "topic_id": "p05-neg-zh-三步法", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "8db71d8b-c699-4d31-b504-0feb7d6fc888", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "第一步", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "p05-8db71d8b-9029", "text": "First validate the input, next normalize the casing, then write the record. The order matters because normalization assumes valid input. Doing it any other way raises confusing errors.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 28, "topic_id": "p05-neg-order-list", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "8db71d8b-c699-4d31-b504-0feb7d6fc888", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "First validate", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "p05-8db71d8b-9030", "text": "The new scheduler is slightly slower on small batches, though it is still comfortably within our latency budget. For the workloads we actually run it is fast enough. I am comfortable keeping it.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 33, "topic_id": "p05-neg-slightly-slower", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "8db71d8b-c699-4d31-b504-0feb7d6fc888", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "though it is still", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
